1
00:00:00,846 --> 00:00:05,862
BoardGuard — an AI microscope assistant for electronics repair technicians.

2
00:00:05,862 --> 00:00:09,632
A representative 3D logic board for navigation. Each region links to real microscope captures.

3
00:00:09,632 --> 00:00:16,391
Scenario 02: a fine-pitch TQFP photographed under a ring light. Processing runs live with OpenCV 5.

4
00:00:16,391 --> 00:00:22,136
Two suspected bridges. C01 sits in a specular hotspot: 28% of its region is glare.

5
00:00:22,136 --> 00:00:28,414
The amber layer is the OpenCV specular mask behind the decision (toggled off, then on).

6
00:00:28,414 --> 00:00:33,457
Rule R-E1: evidence insufficient. The agent asks for a specific new look instead of guessing.

7
00:00:33,457 --> 00:00:41,664
The technician recaptures with diffuse light. The new image is registered to the first one.

8
00:00:41,664 --> 00:00:49,666
Reinspection: the glare suspicion is not reproduced, so its priority drops. C02 persists, so its priority rises.

9
00:00:49,666 --> 00:01:00,738
C02 is a fibre lying across two leads. The technician decides; BoardGuard recommends a continuity check.

10
00:01:00,738 --> 00:01:09,268
Every tool call, rule and human decision is traced, timed and exportable.

11
00:01:09,268 --> 00:01:14,986
Each finding's reinspection outcome is its own decision, citing the rule that fired.

12
00:01:14,986 --> 00:01:31,832
Scenario 03: before/after verification. SIFT + MAGSAC registration with measured residuals.

13
00:01:31,832 --> 00:01:38,049
The difference map shows where the visible change is. It is linked back to each finding.

14
00:01:38,049 --> 00:01:42,772
Visible change is documented. Electrical verification stays with the technician.

15
00:01:42,772 --> 00:01:54,739
Scenario 05: a real rework pair shot from different angles. Alignment is unreliable, so no overlay is drawn.

16
00:01:54,739 --> 00:02:07,594
System: the live OpenCV 5 runtime, the processing environment, tool contracts and reproducible evaluation.

17
00:02:07,594 --> 00:02:12,613
BoardGuard: see the damage, guide the repair, verify the result. A visual aid that knows when to look again.
